And then it learns over time

00:33:52.420 --> 00:33:53.420
itself

00:33:53.520 --> 00:33:55.960
by getting the reward when it
doesn't do that.

00:33:55.960 --> 00:33:57.440
Exactly.
The main idea behind

00:33:57.440 --> 00:33:58.860
reinforcement learning

00:33:58.860 --> 00:34:01.620
is less about predicting y from
x.

00:34:01.620 --> 00:34:05.700
And instead, what it does is it
simulates a bot or an agent in

00:34:05.700 --> 00:34:08.060
an environment.
And it gives it rewards for

00:34:08.060 --> 00:34:10.400
doing the right thing.
And it penalizes it for doing

00:34:10.400 --> 00:34:12.060
the wrong thing.
And the right and wrong thing is

00:34:12.060 --> 00:34:14.240
customized by whoever sets up
the agent.

00:34:14.240 --> 00:34:17.920
And you get it to learn using
positive reinforcement, sort of

00:34:17.920 --> 00:34:21.320
modeled by how children are
given good things when they

00:34:21.320 --> 00:34:24.380
behave well and punished,
hopefully not too poorly,

00:34:25.000 --> 00:34:26.360
when they don't behave well.

00:34:26.360 --> 00:34:28.600
And you hear about reinforcement
learning a lot in the media,

00:34:28.600 --> 00:34:33.140
especially in the context of
these coding agents and the

00:34:33.140 --> 00:34:35.640
